---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FeatureArticle from './editorial/FeatureArticle.astro';
import ArticleOpening from './editorial/ArticleOpening.astro';
import Study from '../previews/adventure/study.mdx';
import source from '../previews/adventure/source.json';
import {gameStudies,GAME_STUDIES_ROOT} from '../data/game-studies.mjs';
import '../styles/adventure-study.css';
const study=gameStudies.find(study=>study.slug==='adventure')!;
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'The Vault',href:'/vault/'},{label:'Game Studies',href:GAME_STUDIES_ROOT},{label:study.title}];
---
<Layout title="Adventure: a world at the other end of a sentence" description={study.description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} noindex={!study.reviewed}>
 <FeatureArticle class="adventure-study">
  <ArticleOpening slot="opening" title={study.title} subtitle={study.subtitle} description={study.description} image={study.image} imageSet="/images/studies/adventure/header-1280.webp 1280w, /images/studies/adventure/header-2172.webp 2172w" imageCredit="Original editorial illustration · an imagined cave" metadata="Colossal Cave · Crowther & Woods · Whole-game study" />
  <nav class="study-contents" aria-label="In this study">
   <p>Explore the study</p>
   <ul>
    <li><a href="#a-road-a-building-and-a-reason-to-investigate">Enter the cave</a></li>
    <li><a href="#what-the-parser-actually-does">Words and parsers</a></li>
    <li><a href="#mapping-landmarks-and-the-pleasure-of-getting-lost">Maps and puzzles</a></li>
    <li><a href="#a-real-cave-two-authors-and-several-kinds-of-imagination">People and places</a></li>
    <li><a href="#from-playing-an-adventure-to-authoring-one">Making adventures</a></li>
    <li><a href="#sources-and-further-reading">Sources</a></li>
   </ul>
  </nav>
  <Study />
  <Fragment slot="ending">
   <p>This study has not yet been fact-checked. Sources and selected execution records accompany the account; the ending has been inspected in source rather than played through.</p>
   <p><em>Adventure</em> game text: Will Crowther and Don Woods. Selected behaviour was checked in Arthur O’Dwyer’s later C port of the 350-point game. Short extracts support criticism and review; rights in the game remain with their owners. The header and explanatory diagrams are original illustrations.</p>
   <p><a href={source.canonical}>Study sources and research notes</a> · <a href={`https://github.com/code198x/docs/blob/${source.revision}/studies/adventure/evidence.md`}>Evidence and limits</a> · <a href={GAME_STUDIES_ROOT}>More game studies</a></p>
  </Fragment>
 </FeatureArticle>
</Layout>
